// The argument kind rule reaches an INTRINSIC signature. A `ParamSig`'s `className` is the C type
// spelling — `paramSigsOf` fills it that way for every declared parameter — but the synthesized
// string/InlineArray signatures left it empty, so the rule was silent on exactly the methods reached
// first. An offset is a `size_t`, per `include/kama_runtime.h`.
fn int32 main() {
    string s = "hello";
    string t = s.substring(start: "no", end: 3);
    return 0;
}
